title: View/Edit Geometry
keyword: EDIT
manual: structure/#c2-edit

Inspect and edit the structure of a system: its species, atoms, unit cell, molecules,
bonds and symmetry. Every change is applied to the system immediately. "Restore" returns
the system to the geometry it had when it was first opened, and "Keep bonding" preserves
the bond connectivity when the geometry changes.

# Tabs
- Species: one row per species. Click the atomic number to move the atoms to another
  species or change the element; "New" adds a species.
- Atoms: the atoms and their coordinates. "Types" groups the atoms by category and "Keep
  symmetry" makes coordinate changes respect the space group. "Expression" evaluates an
  expression at the atomic positions. "All", "None" and "Toggle" change the selection;
  "Add", "Duplicate", "Remove", "Merge" and "Reorder" act on the selected atoms.
- Cell (crystals only): the lattice parameters (a/b/c, α/β/γ, volume) are editable, with
  "Keep symmetry" to keep the space group. "Cell transformations" goes to the conventional,
  primitive, Niggli or Delaunay cell. "Supercells" builds a simple na/nb/nc repetition or
  a full transformation whose lattice vectors can be typed or picked in the view. "Nice
  supercells" lists, up to "Max. size", the supercells with the largest inscribed sphere;
  click a row to apply one.
- Molecules: the molecular fragments with their number of atoms, point group and center of
  mass. Selected molecules can be removed or reordered.
- Bonds: "Bond operations" create, remove or change the order of bonds by clicking in the
  view. "System bonds" lists the bonds of every atom (single, double, triple, aromatic or
  dashed) with a context menu per bond. "Bond calculation" sets the covalent radii, the
  bond factor, the bond delta and the allowed pairs; "Apply" recomputes the connectivity.
- Symmetry: for molecules, the point group and its operations, with "Refine" to move the
  atoms onto their exact symmetry positions. For crystals, the space group, the detection
  tolerance with "Recalculate", "Clear", "Refine" and "Whole Molecules", the operations and
  centering vectors (select them to create a symmetry-elements object or delete them to
  build a subgroup), and "Space group analysis", which scans the space group as a function
  of the tolerance.
